<p align="left" class="body1"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-05 | Tuesday</font></strong><br/><br/><span class="Apple-style-span">What up though. It's all to the woodgrain with your comrade Geo keeping warm and recovering form seasonal virii in the Great Northwest. Between sips of green tea and issues of <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-style: italic">Preacher</span>, been polishing up some rhymes and hooks for the 2nd Blue Scholars album, which we announced for the first time at the 11/22 Showbox show will be dropping <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">MAY 1, 2007</span> and will be titled <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">BAYANI</span>. The album title's meaning will come forth as we put the finishing touches on it later this month and early '07.�</span><div><br><div><span class="Apple-style-span">Safe travels to <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">Saba</span> and <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">RA</span> who are in Bellingham tonight and back in town to rock <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">Neumo's</span> on Wednesday night (12/6) with <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">Dan the Automator</span>. Also, send your love and thoughts to <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">The Coup</span>, <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">Mr. Lif</span> and all the folks who were on tour with them as their tourbus crashed the other day. It was just seven days ago when our tour paths crossed with them in San Francisco. First, Common Market's series of unfortunate tour events and now this proves the saying true: It's kinda dangerous to be an emcee.</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span class="Apple-style-span">One last reminder to the folks in the 509: on Thursday, <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-style: italic">Dec. 7, the entire Mass Line roster will be rocking Spokane, WA at Whitworth College</span>. For our folks in Seattle on the same night, we recommend checking out what's sure to be a phenomenal <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">all-women's hip-hop show at Youngstown Cultural Arts Center</span> in West Seattle. Here are the details:</span></div><div><br/></div><div>"INDAYog: the rhythm in the movement"</div><div>AN ALL WOMENS HIP HOP SHOW�</div><div>proceeds to�benefit Pinay's human rights campaign</div><div><br/></div><div>Thursday</div><div>December 7, 2006</div><div>Doors 8pm | Show 9 pm</div><div><br/></div><div>Youngstown Cultural Arts Center</div><div>4408 Delridge Way SW</div><div>Seattle, WA 98106</div><div><br/></div><div>$10 pre sale - all ages</div><div>tickets:�http://www.brownpapertickets.com/event/8827</div><div><br/></div><div>An all women's hip hop show with performances and art by Skim, Beyond</div><div>Reality, Piece, Cristina Orbe, Sistah Hailstorm, Vivid Vixens, DJ</div><div>Wasabi, Angel179, Baby T, El Dia, Rogue Pinay, CanarySing, Onion,</div><div>Michelle Mukai, DJ Sweet Elite, DJ Mixxstress, Julie C, Southern Komfort, and Maritza</div><div>Soledad</div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div></br></div><p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-05 | Tuesday</font></strong><br/><br/><address>somewhat surprisingly it's been hard to numb the pain caused by a series of unfortunate events out here; just when we think we've gotten over the senseless mourning for material goods, we're reminded of the crime's impact (i don't know if the word is out, but all the lyrics for the new CM album plus more from upcoming compilation projects got lifted, as well - sorry chev, your book is gone).  to add insult to injury, our show in chico was cancelled in the final hour - just after we had mobbed up from santa cruz pushing the speed of sound.<br><br>but last night's show at berbati's was redemption.  thanks to all the good folks who came out and showed love - it was truly needed.<br><br>furthermore, i received the news this morning of the coup's tour bus accident.  our thoughts and prayers are with them, and from this point on i am determined to be thankful in the face of adversity.<br><br>it's all love...<br><br>RA<br> </br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></address><p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-03 | Sunday</font></strong><br/><br/>Good Medicine... that is Geologic, Khingz, Macklemore &amp; Gabriel Teodros, will be taking over Street Sounds tonight from 6 - 9pm on KEXP 90.3 FM, streaming live at http://www.kexp.org<br><br>we'll have a few special guests, some artists &amp; educators, and a healthy dose of underheard classics for your sunday evening.  we'll also be giving out some tickets for Common Market with Dan The Automator, Chali2na, Casual and A.G.  don't miss it!<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-01 | Friday</font></strong><br/><br/>the show last night went well.  got some love from the Bay Area crowd once again when we rocked the stage at the <strong>Mezzanine</strong>.  much love to Jill and her homegirls Irene and Sheila for comin out and helping work merch and keeping these MassLine representatives company.  peace to the folks at <strong>Poleng Lounge</strong> and <strong>Kiwi</strong> for holding it down on N30 in our absence.<br><br>for a minute yesterday, i was concerned that we wouldn't have much interesting news to share with the folks at home about our travels.  but we're in luck!  for the 4 hours that our car was parked at 13th and Mission last night, some folks broke in and helped themselves to our <strong>turntables</strong>, <strong>CDJ</strong>, <strong>mixer</strong>, a few records, headphones, needles, and my new <strong>Crooks &amp; Castles</strong> hoodie from the homie <strong>Rush</strong> at <strong>TRUE</strong>.  who said tour would be boring?<br><br>honestly, we were pretty disappointed for a few hours.   but the truth is, if we can hold our heads up with joy in the face of record poverty and the war in Iraq, a few pieces of missing gear shouldn't be anything to shed a tear about.<br><br><img align="absmiddle" alt="mixer" height="150" title="mixer" width="103"><br><img align="absmiddle" alt="cdj" height="116" title="cdj" width="150"><br><br><img align="absmiddle" alt="turntable" height="69" title="turntable" width="111"><br><br><img alt="hoodie" height="72" src="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/assets/48d094f39752c9b7587e.jpg" title="hoodie" width="96"><br><br>goodbye my friends, you will be missed.<br><br>saba<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-30 | Thursday</font></strong><br/><br/>last nite was the jumpoff for the Dan The Automator tour.  with the crowd being majority college students purveying miller lite behavior, i would probably dub <strong>San Luis Obispo</strong> "the Bellingham of Southern California."  until now, the only thing i knew about "SLO" was that it was shouted out on the single for <strong>Hiero's</strong> <strong>"One Big Trip."</strong><br><br>big up to <strong>Casual</strong>, <strong>AG</strong>, and <strong>Chali 2na</strong> for rockin the stage.  we look forward to sharing the stage with ya'll for the next couple weeks. <br><br>also big up to <strong>House</strong>, <strong>Zion I's</strong> tour manager for making a cameo.  let's get kicked out of a mexican restaurant by a bunch of scared white folks again homie!<br><br>the word of the day is "internettes."  definition? anybody we communicate with via the internet, be it a podcast, blog, or otherwise.<br/><br/>with that, i'd like to leave all you internettes with this little nugget from the past.  i still know the rap from this commercial word for word as i intended to impress all my classmates on the first day of school in 7th grade with it in the cafeteria.<br/><br/>howla.  <br/><br/>-Saba<br/><p class="massline-embed-gap">Archived embedded media is unavailable for offline playback. <a class="massline-external-playback" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7rlBJSycg0s" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open video 7rlBJSycg0s on YouTube (external playback)</a></p><p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><center><div class="pagenumbers"><a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-614e9005b7af.php">[&lt;&lt;]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-ff41e4b899bf.php">[1]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-f09e4ab70de0.php">[2]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-13fd6b501db4.php">[3]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a6d8d32ad781.php">[4]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-d45f54b0cbc4.php">[5]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-0bfc403792bc.php">[6]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-fd78b8847920.php">[7]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-cd30dd4ecbb4.php">[8]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-3f0473af164e.php">[9]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-328a9b624d92.php">[10]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-3c1fe8996261.php">[11]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-86e16e039033.php">[12]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-7e9b30d94f52.php">[13]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a4c814fd9062.php">[14]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinem